First aid for jellyfish stings
1. Perform a scene survey and a primary survey.
2. Apply as much vinegar as possible to the affected area. 
Vinegar will stop the stingers from releasing venom.
3. To help relieve pain, bathe the affected part in warm water, 
as warm as the casualty can tolerate for about 20 minutes.
4. Do not apply cold water. Cold water helps the stingers to 
continue releasing venom.
5. If signs of infection occur, seek medical help.
